    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2018fe1b_40935688",
        "filename": "common/thermal.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 203,
      "author": {
        "id": 1386300
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-16T17:12:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As per the existing code changes and this URL reference, the “dptf_set_fan_duty_target()” function called during the boot-up time and it handovers the Fan control from EC to DPTF, if DPTF is available (common/acpi.c).\nURL: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/master/common/acpi.c#323 \n\nIn current patch code changes (common/thermal.c), we added to call “dptf_set_fan_duty_target()” function to handle the run-time scenarios and to change the current temp cut-off value considering below scenarios. \n- Scenario#1: After the device booted successfully and the control is handed over from EC to DPTF. In this case, if we delete the DPTF related .conf and .so file (for test purpose), the EC has to Handle the control, which will be done by using “DECLARE_HOOK -\u003e thermal_control()” function.\n- Scenario#2: After the scenario#1, if we copy or replace back the deleted DPTF related .conf and *.so files, the EC has to handover the control to DPTF by using “DECLARE_HOOK -\u003e thermal_control()” function. \n- Scenario#3: Inside the DECLARE_HOOK -\u003e thermal_control()” function, we are calling the “dptf_set_fan_duty_target()” function by checking the current temperature + CONFIG_DPTF_FAIL_SAFE_OFFSET value (by using “get_dptf_alive_Statue () function)\n- At the moment, we have declared the “CONFIG_DPTF_FAIL_SAFE_OFFSET” value as “0” and this could be changed in the future code flow to increase the cut off value for current temperature.\n   This current patch works fine and tested on multiple Hatch and Helios systems with above scenarios.",
      "parentUuid": "caf71619_67e39d6a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 200,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 203,
        "endChar": 2
      },
      "revId": "e8278c6049995e73abc3d0baaafa0dfef3929b66",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
